      "content": "The stinging sensation is caused by volatile sulfur compounds released from the onion's cells when they are cut, breaking cell walls. This mechanical damage releases enzymes, notably alliinase, which acts upon sulfur-containing compounds like alliin. This enzymatic reaction leads to the formation of syn-propanethial S-oxide, a highly volatile irritant gas that is trapped in the tears and causes the burning sensation.",
